\f0\fs26 \cf0 The introduction of holo-screen was greeted with much enthusiasm by the meme-centric upper class, breaking all sales records, but they turned out to be a bit of a wank. They were really only useful if you had to examine objects in 3D day. Medicine, architecture, academia and of course the porn industry had a legitimate need for this technology, but few others. Most financial and business records were steadfastly stuck in 2D territory and consequently holo-screens were an unnecessary expense for the average business. In any case, no boss wanted his workers constantly distracted by porn stars, floating above each desk, the money shots where just too life-like. Sales of these devices stalled and then fell off all together. Although most went back to using the glass screen, a standard for decades, porn addicts still had one tucked away at home, for those critical times when the wife was out. }